  "description": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "The study examined whether the first presenting symptom of behavioral variant frontotemporal dementia\u2014apathy or disinhibition\u2014was associated with later neuropsychological profiles, brain atrophy patterns, and classification of patient subgroups.",
   "value_source": "generated"
  },
  "design": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "Cross-sectional evaluation of healthy controls and two patient groups with probable bvFTD, retrospectively classified according to whether apathy or disinhibition was the first symptom, with neuropsychological assessment and 3T structural MRI acquired approximately three years after disease debut. Whole-brain VBM, ROI analyses, correlations, factorial discriminant analysis, and support vector machine classification were used.",
   "value_source": "generated"
  },
